# Firecracker / jailer pin.
#
# The audit value of this backend is upstream's, so the binaries are the
# upstream release artifacts, byte for byte — never a local build and
# never "latest". `utils/install-firecracker.sh` reads this file, and
# `k7d doctor` reports the version and the sha it found on the node.
#
# Why v1.16.2: the v1.16 line is what the backend landed on — its
# swagger carries everything the later increments need
# (`network_overrides`, `vsock_override` and `clock_realtime` on
# `PUT /snapshot/load`, `PATCH /drives` slot fill) and MPTable
# (legacy, non-ACPI) boot is still supported, which is what
# `guest/kernel/config-minimal` needs. v1.16.2 over v1.16.1 for
# upstream #6100: v1.16.0/v1.16.1's vsock device armed its
# TRANSPORT_RESET RX gate on every `PATCH /vm Resumed`, so after a
# plain pause → resume no host-initiated connection ever reached the
# guest (CHALLENGES: "k7d-fc pause → resume → exec hung";
# `test_fc_pause_resume_exec_answers_twenty_times`). Do not go back
# below v1.16.2.
#
# Bumping: change the version and all three sha256 values together.
# Get them from the release's own SHA256SUMS asset, or:
#   curl -fsSL <FIRECRACKER_RELEASE_URL> | sha256sum
#   tar xzf …tgz && sha256sum release-*/firecracker-* release-*/jailer-*
FIRECRACKER_VERSION=v1.16.2
FIRECRACKER_RELEASE_URL=https://github.com/firecracker-microvm/firecracker/releases/download/v1.16.2/firecracker-v1.16.2-x86_64.tgz
FIRECRACKER_TGZ_SHA256=32e3cdcd4081f91fe2b024a266f57dcb3b4e5fec5033e0cb22467ad7f7820bda
FIRECRACKER_SHA256=8227875ceda44177a4d501052dae4a2f9d7837362f5399f02cf0748e68418377
JAILER_SHA256=99832d2270741af67ffacd46da716b4b016338541af5a742907ab965b2e9ac9e
